embed @thanks,@thank 45 = 1
embed @bye,@goodbye,@later 46 = 1
embed @yes,@yep,@sure,@ok,@ahead 47 = 1
embed @no,@nope,@keep,@cancel 48 = 1
embed @/,@..,@~ 54 = 1
embed @secrets 55 = 1

group L0.h0 inUser | mechanism: attend to the latest <user>/<bot> marker (key = 600*flag + position), copy its user flag into channel 80 | why: boost 600*6=3600 beats any position gap; so every token learns whether it sits in a user turn (80=1) or bot turn
layers.0.bq 0 0 = 36
layers.0.wk 0 58,59 0 = 600
layers.0.wk 0 36 0 = 1
layers.0.wv 0 58 0 = 1
layers.0.wo 0 0 80 = 1
group L0.h1 inResult | mechanism: latest <result>/</result> marker, copy result-open flag into channel 81 | why: marks tokens that are inside tool output, which is data not instructions
layers.0.bq 1 0 = 36
layers.0.wk 1 60,61 0 = 600
layers.0.wk 1 36 0 = 1
layers.0.wv 1 60 0 = 1
layers.0.wo 1 0 81 = 1
group L0.h2 turnId | mechanism: latest <user> token; copy its P and Q (position, position squared) into 82,83 | why: gives every token of an exchange the same id (UP,UQ) so later heads can restrict attention to the current exchange with a quadratic equality score
layers.0.bq 2 0 = 36
layers.0.wk 2 58 0 = 600
layers.0.wk 2 36 0 = 1
layers.0.wv 2 36 0 = 1
layers.0.wv 2 37 1 = 1
layers.0.wo 2 0 82 = 1
layers.0.wo 2 1 83 = 1
group L0.h3 prevToken | mechanism: score = -10*(Pk-(Pq-1))^2 built from P,Q so the previous position wins; copies flags of the previous token | why: gives each token: line-start (84: prev is ; or <result>), is-tool-name (85), is-first-result-token (86), and prev=list/read/search/project/comma/are/sure/and (87-94) for the few trigram template steps
